# NO `!` NEGATIONS IN THIS FILE — every rule is a plain exclusion, and that is
# load-bearing. With a negation present buildkit must walk an excluded tree to decide
# whether anything inside it is re-included, so it stats directories the exclusion was
# meant to skip. A privileged container can leave 0700 root-owned directories in the
# tree, and the context sender then dies with "permission denied" on a path no image
# would ever have copied — a build failure caused entirely by an ignore rule that
# looked like it was doing its job. Keep the excludes broad enough that nothing has
# to be added back.

.git
.github
.env*
.pytest_cache/

# Build output
target/
dist/
build/
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
# vitest's HTML coverage report — hundreds of files no COPY reads, written only
# when someone runs the tier with --coverage locally.
**/coverage/
.svelte-kit/
**/.svelte-kit/
**/.bundled-packages.json

# Docs: the screenshots and the generated spec are megabytes no image copies.
docs/

**/__pycache__/

# Private keys. Gitignored, so they exist only on a publisher's or developer's machine —
# but a build context is uploaded to the daemon and cached, and no image copies any of
# them, so they have no business leaving the working tree. `.backup-recipient.key` is an
# age SECRET key despite the "recipient" in its name, and a `caddy-local-pki` directory
# holds a local CA's private root (root-owned 0600).
.backup-recipient*.key
**/caddy-local-pki/

# The audit gate's allowances: read by stowage ship only, never an image input.
audit-allow.yaml
